@startuml git-branches-and-blame-state
title E2 — merge_branch Decision Flow

[*] --> Analyzing : merge_branch(name)

Analyzing --> UpToDate : name's tip already\nan ancestor of HEAD
UpToDate --> [*]

Analyzing --> FastForward : fast-forward possible\n(HEAD is an ancestor of name)
FastForward --> [*] : HEAD ref moved,\nsafe checkout run,\nno commit created

Analyzing --> RealMerge : neither up-to-date\nnor fast-forwardable

RealMerge --> Conflicted : repo.merge() leaves\nindex conflicts
RealMerge --> CleanMerge : repo.merge() leaves\na clean index

CleanMerge --> Merged : commit()\n(MERGE_HEAD-aware,\ndefault message)
Merged --> [*]

Conflicted --> Resolving : returned to caller\nas MergeOutcome::Conflicts(paths)
Resolving --> Resolving : resolve_conflict()\nper path\n(existing E1 flow,\nsee git-support-state.puml)
Resolving --> Merged : every path resolved,\nuser presses Commit\n(same commit() call,\nMERGE_HEAD-aware)

@enduml
